in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @ui
in @nl
in @labeled
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction

# @docs — the typed-document substrate family-root.
#
# Recognition #96 candidate territory (continuing from @ui at
# `shards/ui.mirror`, Mara Phase C, 2026-06-23): instrument-altitude
# vs presentation-altitude is a real substrate partition. @ui declared
# the INSTRUMENT side (mote/arc/field/rgba8_buffer/spectral_gpu); the
# eigenboard substance. @docs declares the PRESENTATION side: the
# typed document that COMPOSES instrument output with linguistic
# content into a renderable page.
#
# === What this family declares ===
#
# Per Alex 2026-06-23 (Loop Phase D directive):
#
#   @docs combines @ui (instrument) + @nl (linguistic content) as
#   substrate-decl. Presentation altitude; TEA loosely inspires the
#   composition pattern at @docs/tea (NOT @code/elm).
#
# So this family-root names the SHAPE of a typed page: an ordered
# composition of content blocks (some textual via @nl, some
# instrument-rendered via @ui, some compositional/structural) that
# together discharge into a single rendered_page artifact.
#
# Five primitives, each a Prism per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-
# as-everything]]:
#
#   document         a complete typed-document instance; the unit
#                    @docs operates on end-to-end
#   content_block    a typed section / paragraph / aside / widget;
#                    the COMPOSITION ATOM of a document
#   page_state       the current rendering state (which sections
#                    open, scroll position, interactive-widget
#                    state); the typed mutable surface @docs/tea
#                    consumes as `model`
#   rendered_page    the rendered output + provenance — typed as
#                    `labeled(rgba8_buffer, document)` per the
#                    labeled<> functor primitive landed today at
#                    `shards/labeled.mirror`; the projection back
#                    to the source document IS the provenance
#                    contract
#   perturbation     re-imported from @glass for signatures (NOT
#                    re-declared)
#
# === The composition workflow (per woz:explore earlier today) ===
#
# @docs IS a transformation workflow, NOT a pure functor. The shape:
#
#   text (corpus @nl)
#     -> spectral triple (the typed structural decomposition;
#        sections, references, glossary edges, sidenote anchors)
#     -> field construction (instrument-altitude @ui scenes for
#        any embedded eigenboard widgets)
#     -> @ui render (the actual rgba8 pixels for instrument parts)
#     -> presentation composition (typography + layout + instrument
#        embedding into one page)
#     -> rendered_page (the labeled artifact carrying both pixels
#        and provenance)
#
# The workflow is NOT a single functor application — it is a
# multi-altitude transformation where each step lives at its own
# substrate altitude and the composition between altitudes happens
# at @docs. That is what makes this family-root load-bearing: it
# names the composition SURFACE, not the composition formula.
#
# === Recognition #96 candidate territory ===
#
# Continuing from @ui's hedge 6: the partition "instrument-altitude
# vs presentation-altitude" needs a second witness to promote. @docs
# IS the second witness — the same partition, lifted to the
# presentation side. The candidate is now ratifiable IF Pack agrees
# the partition is structural (not just a delivery-target convenience).
#
# Forward-promised: third witness from @audio (if it ever lands)
# would close the recognition; ratification gate per
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] requires structural
# independence of witnesses, which @ui/@docs satisfy (one is the
# substance-renderer; the other is the typography-composer; they
# are not the same family lifted twice).
#
# === Forward-promised consumers ===
#
# - shards/docs/tea.mirror (LANDS IN THIS COMMIT). The TEA-shaped
#   composition pattern at presentation-altitude; canonical
#   implementor will be Gleam Lustre via cascade<gleam, js> per
#   Mara research at c486718. NOT @code/elm — that grammar is
#   deferred per §6 of the research doc.
# - spectral.engineer/case-study/X (per Alex 2026-06-23 deployment
#   cascade); the first applied @docs consumer. The case-study
#   substrate composes @ui-rendered eigenboard panels with @docs-
#   rendered narrative; this family supplies the narrative-side
#   composition surface.
# - Future @docs/sidenotes (per Tufte sidenote pattern;
#   forward-promised at Phase E briefs); a species shard that
#   specializes content_block with the sidenote-anchor carrier.
# - Future @docs/glossary (per spectral.engineer corpus needs);
#   another content_block species specialization.
# - spectral TUI eigenboard view (docs/specs/tui-v0.md); same @docs
#   primitives, different rendered_page shape (terminal cell grid
#   vs RGBA8 buffer; the labeled<> functor accommodates both with
#   a different first type parameter).
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - #96 candidate territory: this is the second-witness shard. @ui
#   surfaced the partition; @docs ratifies it from the other side.
# - #93 H4 (labeled<> functor primitive; RESOLVED 2026-06-23 at
#   `shards/labeled.mirror`): rendered_page = labeled(rgba8_buffer,
#   document) IS the 5th load-bearing labeled<> instance landing
#   today (after StageFreight npm_artifact, @cascade loss_lens,
#   @cogito name_output, and the canonical labeled<> shard itself).
#   The provenance contract IS the labeled functor at the page
#   altitude.
# - #50 form/substance partition (Bateson 1970): @docs operates at
#   the form altitude (typography, layout, structure); the @ui
#   embeds bring substance (eigenboard motes are the matter being
#   rendered) into the form scaffold. Adjacent Bateson levels.
# - #55 form/process partition at family-root altitude: @docs is
#   form-side at the presentation altitude; @docs/tea (this commit)
#   is process-side at the same altitude. The split lives WITHIN
#   the family — same recognition #55 pattern as @mirror vs
#   @kintsugi.
# - #57 alignment as boundary mathematics at @io: the SSR vs
#   client-side rendering boundary IS an @io altitude; @docs's
#   render_doc action is form-side; the actual byte emission at
#   network or screen happens at @io.
# - #59 kintsugi loop altitude-portable: @docs's composed bilateral
#   (docs_complete) follows the same composed-bilateral pattern as
#   @cascade.cascade_well_defined, @ui.ui_instrument_coherent,
#   confirming the discipline at one more altitude.
# - #95 @cascade family-root: @docs's delivery to browser IS
#   cascade<gleam, js> via Lustre per research doc; this family
#   supplies the typed_source grammar that cascade measures.
#
# === Honest hedges ===
#
# 1. The composition shape is NOT a pure functor. text -> document
#    is a transformation workflow with multiple non-commutative
#    steps (section extraction, anchor resolution, instrument
#    embedding, layout). The substrate-decl carries the SURFACE
#    primitives (carriers + actions + bilaterals); the per-page
#    composition recipe lives at the instance altitude. Conflating
#    "the substrate names the composition" with "the substrate
#    fully computes the composition" would be the error.
#
# 2. SSR vs client-side rendering is the substantive partition this
#    shard does NOT resolve. render_doc returns a rendered_page;
#    whether those bytes get emitted server-side and shipped as HTML
#    or computed client-side via Lustre's JS bundle is a CASCADE-
#    SPECIES decision, not a @docs-altitude one. The Universal
#    Components pattern (Lustre 5.6.0) lets one source ship both;
#    the substrate-decl admits both modes without forcing the
#    choice.
#
# 3. content_block is genuinely polymorphic. A paragraph of @nl
#    text, a Tufte sidenote, an embedded @ui eigenboard widget, a
#    glossary cross-reference — all four are content_blocks but
#    they discharge differently. The substrate-decl carries
#    content_block as `ref` (parametric at the floor); species
#    shards (`shards/docs/sidenotes.mirror`, etc.) will specialize.
#    For now the polymorphism is documentation-altitude only.
#
# 4. The provenance contract (rendered_page carrying back-reference
#    to source document via labeled<>) requires that document
#    instances be content-addressed. The substrate already has the
#    OID infrastructure (per @mirror/store + uuid.mirror); this
#    shard ASSUMES content-addressing exists. Forward-promised:
#    if a document is mutated mid-render (long-running interactive
#    page), the labeled<> back-reference must carry the version
#    that was rendered, not the current head. Discharge happens at
#    species altitude.
#
# 5. Recognition #96 candidate is still un-ratified at commit time.
#    The promotion gate (per Seam adversarial review pattern) needs
#    Pack agreement. This shard lands as substrate-decl regardless;
#    the recognition canonical doc is a separate forward-promise
#    at `docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-96-instrument-altitude-
#    vs-presentation-altitude-candidate.md` (referenced from
#    `shards/ui.mirror` already; this shard extends the same
#    candidate territory).
#
# 6. The "text -> spectral triple" step (workflow stage 2) currently
#    has no substrate primitive. Sections, references, glossary
#    edges, sidenote anchors are all content_block specializations
#    we forward-promise; the EDGES BETWEEN them (the spectral
#    triple's H component for the document) are not yet named at
#    substrate altitude. Mara survey altitude finding: this might
#    be the recognition that emerges from extending @docs further.
#    Flagged for Pack review.
#
# Spec context: docs/research/2026-06-23-elm-architecture-and-code-
#               elm-substrate-decl.md (Mara research; commit c486718;
#               §5 declares the @docs/tea sketch this family-root
#               grounds; §6 recommends @docs/tea over @code/elm at
#               substrate-decl altitude);
#               docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-96-instrument-
#               altitude-vs-presentation-altitude-candidate.md
#               (forward-promised canonical doc; this shard is
#               second-witness substrate-decl-altitude surface).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (document /
#                       content_block / page_state / rendered_page
#                       are separate carriers for separate concepts;
#                       NOT one ref with a discriminator),
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                       (any loss in the text -> document transform
#                       is composite of @epistemologic/properties at
#                       the realisation boundary),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; SSR vs client-side IS
#                       the @io boundary at this altitude),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (the rendered_page = labeled<> instance is
#                       the 5th load-bearing labeled<> witness today;
#                       the parametric carrier was already there).
# Recognition ancestry: #96 candidate territory (second-witness side);
#                       #93 H4 (labeled<> primitive; 5th load-bearing
#                       instance today); #50 form/substance partition;
#                       #55 form/process partition at family-root
#                       altitude; #57 alignment as boundary
#                       mathematics; #59 kintsugi loop altitude-
#                       portable; #95 @cascade family-root.
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/docs.mirror` declares
# `@docs` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @code/rust
source @code/gleam
source @arxiv/programming-languages/wadler-1989-theorems-for-free
source @arxiv/typography/tufte-2001-visual-display

prism @docs {
  focus content
  project structure
  split section
  shift render
  settle commit
}

# === The document carrier ===
#
# A complete typed-document instance: the unit @docs operates on
# end-to-end. Carries the ordered composition of content blocks,
# the global metadata (title, author, version), and the cross-
# reference graph (the spectral triple's H component for the
# document — see hedge 6).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref. Documents
# ARE content-addressed (see hedge 4); two byte-identical documents
# render byte-identically.
type document = ref

# === The content_block carrier ===
#
# A typed atom of document composition: paragraph, section heading,
# Tufte sidenote, embedded eigenboard widget, glossary cross-
# reference. The polymorphism is genuine (hedge 3); species shards
# specialize.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type content_block = ref

# === The page_state carrier ===
#
# The current rendering state: which sections are open, scroll
# position, interactive-widget state, embedded eigenboard's current
# field. The typed mutable surface @docs/tea (companion shard in
# this commit) consumes as its `model` carrier.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type page_state = ref

# === The rendered_page carrier ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed carrier. Per recognition #93 H4
# (labeled<> functor primitive landed today at shards/labeled.mirror):
#
#   rendered_page = labeled(rgba8_buffer, document)
#
# The labeled<> functor pairs the rendered pixels with the source
# document as provenance. unlabel(rendered_page) projects back to
# the rgba8_buffer; label_of(rendered_page) projects back to the
# source document; both projections are substrate-typed.
#
# This is the 5th load-bearing labeled<> instance landing today
# (after StageFreight npm_artifact, @cascade loss_lens, @cogito
# name_output, and the canonical labeled<> shard). The
# substrate-already-had-the-word recognition holds at the page
# altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying labeled<> ref.
type rendered_page = labeled(rgba8_buffer, document)

# === compose action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Takes a natural-language corpus, a
# field (the @ui instrument scene for any embedded widgets), and
# a perturbation; returns a typed document.
#
# This is workflow stage 1+2+3 collapsed into one substrate
# primitive: text -> spectral triple -> field construction. The
# realisation-boundary body discharges the actual section
# extraction, anchor resolution, widget embedding.
#
# Per hedge 1: the substrate-decl carries the SURFACE; the
# composition RECIPE per-document lives at the instance altitude.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
compose(corpus: nl_literal, field: field, p: perturbation) -> document { \ }

# === field_from_measurement action (Phase F-hedge discharge; 2026-06-23) ===
#
# THE BRIDGE PRIMITIVE Mara F flagged as missing (per shards/docs/tea/
# spectral-engineer-case-study.mirror §10 hedge 2): the pipeline from
# @nl.project_measurement output → @ui field construction had no
# substrate-typed primitive between @nl's measurement output and @ui's
# field input. The compose action above takes (corpus, field, p), but
# the field had to come from somewhere; before this action, that
# somewhere was prose-bridged.
#
# This action closes the gap: takes a typed @nl measurement (the
# output of project_measurement: a Connes distance + spectral structure
# typed reference); returns a typed @ui field (motes for token clusters;
# arcs for significant discourse relations; mote colors derived from
# affect_profile when present).
#
# requires measurement_well_formed: the substrate forecloses field
# construction from an ill-defined measurement.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; per-cascade species
# (e.g., the spectral.engineer/case-study/X instance) implement the
# specific mote-placement + arc-strength derivation algorithm.
field_from_measurement(measurement: ref, p: perturbation) -> field
requires measurement_well_formed(measurement, p)
{ \ }

# === render_doc action ===
#
# THE OUTPUT-PRODUCING ACTION. Takes a document + perturbation;
# returns a rendered_page (the labeled<> artifact carrying both
# pixels and provenance).
#
# requires document_well_formed(doc, p): the substrate forecloses
# rendering an ill-formed document. Composition coherence is
# verified before pixels are committed.
#
# Per hedge 2: whether the rendering executes server-side or
# client-side is a CASCADE-SPECIES decision; this action's signature
# admits both modes.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
render_doc(doc: document, p: perturbation) -> rendered_page
requires document_well_formed(doc, p)
{ \ }

# === section action ===
#
# Project a named section out of a document. Substrate-vocabulary
# primitive for accessing the composition atoms by name. Composes
# with the spectral triple's H component (hedge 6): the edges
# between content_blocks form a navigable structure.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
section(doc: document, name: ref, p: perturbation) -> content_block { \ }

# === document_well_formed bilateral ===
#
# Commitment that a document is composition-coherent: all
# content_blocks are typed correctly; all cross-references resolve;
# the section graph has no orphaned anchors; embedded @ui fields
# discharge field_well_formed (from @ui).
#
# Splinter-pole: every block typed, every anchor resolved, no
# orphans; render_doc can proceed.
# Narcissus-pole: missing block type, unresolved anchor, broken
# embed; rendering blocked.
# Narcissus-warned: anchors resolve but to deprecated targets;
# document renders with sidenote-level warnings.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
document_well_formed(doc: document, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === composition_coherent bilateral ===
#
# Commitment that compose's three inputs (corpus, field,
# perturbation) compose coherently: the corpus references resolve
# against the field's eigenboard widgets where applicable; the
# perturbation does not invalidate either side; the resulting
# document satisfies document_well_formed.
#
# Splinter-pole: all three inputs coherently composable; compose
# returns a well-formed document.
# Narcissus-pole: corpus references a widget the field does not
# contain; perturbation breaks the composition invariant.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
composition_coherent(corpus: nl_literal, field: field, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === measurement_well_formed bilateral (Phase F-hedge discharge; 2026-06-23) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that an @nl measurement ref (output of
# project_measurement) carries the structural data needed for field
# construction: token clusters identifiable; significant discourse
# relations bounded; optional affect_profile properly typed.
#
# Splinter-pole: measurement well-formed for @ui field construction;
# Narcissus-pole: measurement missing structural data; field construction
# undefined.
measurement_well_formed(measurement: ref, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === docs_complete composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at the @docs altitude. Same
# composed-bilateral pattern as @cascade.cascade_well_defined and
# @ui.ui_instrument_coherent — three requires + uses labeled<>
# projection where carriers compose (rendered_page IS a labeled<>
# instance; this bilateral's verdict ratifies the labeling).
#
# All three sub-predicates must hold for the @docs cycle (compose
# -> render_doc -> output) to operate end-to-end. Composes
# document_well_formed (output side) + composition_coherent (input
# side) + the @ui's field_well_formed (instrument side, when an
# embedded field is present).
#
# Splinter-pole: all three discharge; @docs cycle complete; the
# rendered_page's labeled<> projection is provenance-valid.
# Narcissus-pole: any sub-predicate fails; cycle blocked at the
# failing altitude.
# Narcissus-warned: all three discharge but at least one is warned
# (e.g., document_well_formed warns deprecated anchors; @docs
# operates with bounded provenance).
#
# Same composed-bilateral discipline pattern as @cascade and @ui;
# altitude-portable per recognition #59.
docs_complete(corpus: nl_literal, field: field, doc: document, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires composition_coherent(corpus, field, p)
requires document_well_formed(doc, p)
requires field_well_formed(field, p)
{ \ }

out @docs
out document
out content_block
out page_state
out field_from_measurement
out measurement_well_formed
out rendered_page
out compose
out render_doc
out section
out document_well_formed
out composition_coherent
out docs_complete
